    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Growth Product Marketing team helps people discover, adopt, and get lasting value from ChatGPT’s consumer paid plans. We partner with Product and teams across Marketing to turn customer insight into subscriber and revenue growth. About the Role We’re hiring a senior product marketer to own growth marketing strategy and execution for ChatGPT’s consumer paid plans. You’ll partner closely with Growth ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Growth Product Marketing team helps people discover, adopt, and get lasting value from ChatGPT’s consumer paid plans. We partner with Product and teams across Marketing to turn customer insight into subscriber and revenue growth. About the Role We’re hiring a senior product marketer to own growth marketing strategy and execution for ChatGPT’s consumer paid plans. You’ll partner closely with Growth Product to turn customer insight into experiments and campaigns, bringing deep expertise in pricing, packaging, and monetization. You’ll own revenue and growth goals across conversion, activation, engagement, retention, and upgrades. In this role, you will: Lead product marketing for pricing and packaging, using research to inform tiers, features, and offers. Lead coordinated launches and customer communications for pricing and plan changes. Own positioning and value propositions for paid plans, using customer research, behavioral data, and competitive insight to define audiences, plan differentiation, and priority use cases. Turn new product capabilities into reasons to subscribe, engage, or upgrade. Drive hands-on execution across in-product experiences, pricing pages, email, and push, writing briefs and copy and coordinating channel owners. Develop and test promotions and growth campaigns that drive paid conversion and upgrades, owning audience strategy, messaging, and measurement. Build lifecycle programs that improve onboarding, feature adoption, engagement, retention, and winback. Partner with Data Science and Finance to measure incremental growth and revenue impact, and use results to scale, improve, or stop programs. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 10+ years of experience in product marketing, growth, or monetization, including substantial experience with subscriptions. Bring deep experience in pricing and packaging, from research and recommendations through launch, with measurable business impact. Have led product marketing for subscriptions, with direct ownership of revenue and growth goals across paid conversion, activation, retention, and upgrades. Bring fluency in funnels, cohort analysis, experimentation, and subscription economics. Combine clear positioning and strong writing with hands-on delivery of briefs, messaging, and campaigns that make complex products easy to understand. Set direction independently, align senior stakeholders, and unblock delivery across teams. You’re hands-on, responsive to evidence, and committed to customer trust. Location: San Francisco, CA. This role requires a hybrid schedule with an in office requirement from Monday - Wednesday. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
